  "verdict": "CLOSED. No aggregation beats first-occurrence anywhere. The largest gain is +.004 (HiTab S2) and AIT-QA and RealHitBench both LOSE by .009 and .031.",
  "why_it_fails": "A question asks about ONE cell. The table holding the best matching cell is the table that holds the answer, and averaging its other cells in only adds noise -- which is why every rule that widens K (top5, top10, count_top200) gets monotonically worse on all four measurements.",
  "consequence": "The half of the cap verdict's next step that said 'reranking / table voting' is closed. What remains of that row is reducing the tables in context WITHOUT paying recall, and the only way left is arrangement rather than selection -- PREREG-2026-08-26-group-context.md."
